  "summary": "Moving Target\nIn an effort to head off a potential collapse in the oil market, the Organization of Petroleum Exporting Countries (OPEC) has moved their November meeting ahead to next week. The market has already begun to speculate that the general softening in crude oil prices means a cut in production is afoot. Meanwhile, future demand picture for crude oil remains clouded by the uncertainty of economic recession in key consuming markets - particularly the United States.",
